.SH "MCP SERVER"
.B duscope mcp
serves saved scans to a Model Context Protocol client over stdin and
stdout, in JSON\-RPC, one message a line, in both the 2026\-07\-28 and the
2025\-11\-25 revisions of the protocol.
It answers from the same saved scans, in the same JSON envelope, as the
command line, in the index directory the command line would use, and opens
no network socket.
Nothing but the protocol's messages goes to stdout; the log goes to
stderr, at the level
.B \-\-log\-level
sets.
.SS Roots
.B \-\-roots
is required and names the directories the client may reach; it can be
given several.
A path outside the roots, one that holds
.BR .. ,
or one longer than 4096 bytes is refused with
.BR refused_path .
A path is resolved as the file system resolves it before it is compared
with the roots, so a link inside a root that leads out of it is refused
too.
A saved scan of a directory under a root is seen as it is, one of a
directory above a root is read at that root, and any other is not seen.
.SS Tools
The server lists the tools below.
A result is the
.B \-\-json
envelope of the verb of the same name, and a tool takes each flag it
exposes as the parameter of the same name in snake case:
.B \-\-min\-size
is
.BR min_size .
.TP
.B duscope_scan
Scan a directory under the roots and save the scan: the other tools read
saved scans.
With
.BR max_age ,
a recent scan of the directory is returned instead.
.TP
.B duscope_scans
The saved scans of directories under the roots, newest first.
.TP
.B duscope_summary
Totals under a path in a saved scan.
.TP
.B duscope_top
The largest directories, or files, under a path.
.TP
.B duscope_by_type
The bytes under a path by kind of file.
.TP
.B duscope_stale
Large files neither modified nor changed for a long time.
.TP
.B duscope_caches
The regenerable caches under a path, with what regenerates each.
.TP
.B duscope_diff
What changed between two saved scans of one tree.
.TP
.B duscope_explain
The facts about one file or directory, with the
.B handle
.B duscope_delete
asks for.
.TP
.B duscope_schema
The index's tables, for
.BR duscope_query ,
or a verb's output as JSON Schema.
.TP
.B duscope_query
One read\-only SQL SELECT over a saved scan, in the command line's
sandbox.
.TP
.B duscope_delete
Only with
.BR \-\-allow\-delete :
move entries under the roots to the Trash, never deleting them.
Each item names a
.B handle
from
.B duscope_explain
and the bytes it should free; a figure off by more than 1% refuses it, and
one refused item stops the call.
A call is a dry run unless
.B dry_run
is false, and the tool asks the client to have a person confirm each call,
which a client that honours it does.
.SS Limits
One call runs at a time, and the rest wait in order.
.B duscope_scan
has 10 minutes and the other tools 30 seconds; a call past its deadline
is answered
.BR deadline_exceeded ,
and a scan past it, or cancelled, saves nothing.
A message is at most 1 MiB.
At most 64 requests, holding 32 MiB between them, wait behind the running
call; one more is answered at once with the JSON\-RPC error \-31000, the
server is busy.
If duscope panics, the server answers the running call and every one
waiting with an internal error (\-32603) before it ends.
.SS Registering
Each client takes one command:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
claude mcp add \-\-transport stdio duscope \-\- duscope mcp \-\-roots ~
codex mcp add duscope \-\- duscope mcp \-\-roots ~
gemini mcp add \-\-scope user duscope duscope mcp \-\- \-\-roots ~
.RE
.fi
.PP
Each tool's parameters, and a Claude Code hook that asks before
.B duscope clean
runs, are in
.IR docs/mcp.md ,
in the source distribution.
